
##  Hardware Design: Rev A Schematic

The schematic captures a highly efficient synchronous buck converter stepping down a nominal 12V automotive/battery input rail to a regulated 5.06V auxiliary output rail capable of supplying up to 3A.

###  PCB Layout: Pre-Routing Floorplan
Prior to drawing copper tracks, components were grouped into logical functional "neighborhoods" to optimize electrical performance and signal integrity. The placement follows a strict left-to-right power flow architecture, prioritizing an ultra-tight input "hot loop" (C5 to VIN/PGND) to minimize high-frequency switching noise. Sensitive analog control elements, such as the feedback divider network (Rtop and R2), are physically isolated on the opposite side of the controller IC, using the chip body as a natural shield against the magnetic fields generated by the power inductor (L1).
